# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR
#
# It is the environment variable TEMPLATE: it says WHAT the project needs, not
# what the values are. It gets copied to `.env.local` and the values are filled
# in there.
#
# ⚠️ THIS FILE DOES GO INTO GIT. `.env.local` DOES NOT: it is covered by the
# `.env*` in `.gitignore`, line 8.
#
# ⚠️ RULE: NO secret is ever pasted here. A secret variable is left EMPTY with
# a comment saying where to get it. The only things that can have a value are
# data that is already public (an email address printed on the site, the
# domain URL).
#
# If this file ever ends up with a key in it, deleting it in a new commit is
# not enough: it stays in the history and the key has to be ROTATED.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Resend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The API key already exists as a SHARED ENV VAR on Vercel: it is not pasted
# here or committed. Locally, copy this file to `.env.local` and paste the key
# there.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Sender. It has to be a VERIFIED domain in Resend; otherwise Resend rejects
# the submission.
#
# ⚠️ IT IS @restoexp.com AND NOT @eatdrinkparadise.com. restoexp.com is the
# ONLY verified domain in the company's Resend account (juanitos and yava use
# the same one). Until 2026-09-23 this said events@eatdrinkparadise.com, which
# Resend would have rejected on the first send. Whoever receives it still
# replies to the right person: every email goes out with `replyTo` = the email
# of whoever wrote in.
RESEND_FROM="Rooftop at Riverside Website <rooftop@restoexp.com>"

# ── Where each form goes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One or more addresses separated by commas. If one is missing,
# `lib/inboxes.ts` falls back to the public inbox in `lib/brand.ts`, so it is
# never left without a destination. The values are the inboxes
# eatdrinkparadise.com publishes today (see the note in `lib/inboxes.ts`).
# They are not secrets: they are printed on the site.
#
#   /contact (everything except «Working here»)
MAIL_TO_CONTACT=info@eatdrinkparadise.com
#   /events, the private event inquiry
MAIL_TO_EVENTS=events@eatdrinkparadise.com
#   /join-us job lane, and /contact with «Working here»
MAIL_TO_CAREERS=hiring@eatdrinkparadise.com
#   /market, the vendor spot application
MAIL_TO_MARKET=info@eatdrinkparadise.com
#   /join-us artist lane
MAIL_TO_BOOKING=info@eatdrinkparadise.com

# ── Newsletter ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️ BLOCKING PENDING ITEM: THIS URL DOES NOT EXIST YET. Without it, the
# pre-footer form validates and returns a visible error, but the signup is NOT
# saved anywhere. The step by step for creating the spreadsheet and publishing
# the Apps Script is in `docs/client-requests.md`.
#
# ⚠️ It is NOT one of the expensive secrets (it is a published Apps Script
# URL, with no token) but it still isn't pasted here: whoever has the URL can
# write rows to the client's spreadsheet.
#
# ⚠️ And there is NO `NEWSLETTER_INBOX`. It was declared from an earlier
# version that sent one email per signup with Resend. One email per signup is
# not a list: someone had to copy the addresses by hand before anything could
# be sent.
NEWSLETTER_SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ── Content ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is no database. Contact, hours, menus, events, openings and blog live
# in the JSON files in `src/content/` (see README). No variable is needed to
# read them.
